#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124353 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/id #uuid "e8f30d47-bfd2-50ea-b2ad-d474e2a58d29" :question/math-academy-id "e-5598" :question/problem "There are two groups of people in a particular city: those who use their own vehicles and those who use public transport. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- $35\\%$ of people who used their own vehicles swap to public transport, and\n\n- $25\\%$ of people who used public transport swap to their own vehicles.\n\nGive the stochastic matrix that describes how people change their means of transportation each year." :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year: \n\n- $35\\%$ of people who used their own vehicles swap to public transport. This implies that $65\\%$ of them remain using their own vehicles.\n\n- $25\\%$ of people who used public transport swap to their own vehicles. This implies that $75\\%$ of them remain using public transport.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Vehicles** | **Public Transport ** |\n| To: | **Vehicles** | $0.65$ | $0.25$ |\n| **Public Transport** | $0.35$ | $0.75$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n![](images/b2/b21fee1abe56dcfdc687be14278c62a20d201ff00e96f1e5918ce22d9dc8b03c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124354 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/id #uuid "95a45716-8c29-5955-af3c-43b6344912da" :question/math-academy-id "e-5599" :question/problem "A certain industry produces $2$ types of sugar, namely sugar $A$ and sugar $B$. The following table describes how the number of consumers changes between both types of sugar in a month:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Sugar $A$** | **Sugar $B$** |\n| To: | **Sugar $A$** | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sugar $B$** | $0.7$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nThat is, $70\\%$ of sugar $A$ customers switch to sugar $B$ each month, and $45\\%$ of sugar $B$ customers switch to sugar $A.$\n\nCurrently, $600$ customers use sugar $A,$ while $400$ customers use sugar $B.$ How many customers will use sugar $A$ in one month? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n![](images/45/451b82e8cb00ede7b0ddf73f35c0555d0eeeeefc5beb5ce4fddd54f0df5f2577.png)\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of sugar is\n![](images/56/56952aeed1d718033af8a3e6d09e8e269f1d70aa8dc31609b8289f025f2e6bd6.png)\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n![](images/ca/cae1bed6b8b01b3ff66c2e8bacf7a10f6c0ece53f3aeac0fb1a51e8fc3c07e8e.png)\n\nTo find the state vector $\\mathbf{x}_1$ after one month, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_1=P\\mathbf{x}_0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.55\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.36 \\\\ 0.64\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one month, $\\color{blue}36\\%$ of customers will use sugar $A.$ Computing $36\\%$ of $1\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000 \\cdot 0.36 = 360.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $360$ customers will use sugar $A$ in one month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124363 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "09540ff7-0444-5169-b582-471be2f1972d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5971" :question/problem "![](images/16/165917feacd28344502759fc6e03f96c5b54d9530701916b746fc489374a6d0b.png) \n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector $\\mathbf{x}_0$ given above. Calculate the state vector $\\mathbf{x}_2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector $\\mathbf{x}_2,$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x_1}=P\\mathbf{x}_0, \\qquad \\mathbf{x}_2=P\\mathbf{x}_1\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 \\\\ 0.8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.18 \\\\ 0.82\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.18 \\\\ 0.82\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.172 \\\\ 0.828\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "25622a0e-3e5b-5f09-bef6-afaa30d153d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-9162" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n![](images/70/70ee929c71d89a443d3ea0efc39ed225f344685059b86a04285a118a476da0f8.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $\\bf{U}$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-0.2 & 0 \\\\ 1.2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $\\bf{V}$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0.35 & 0.95 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.05\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{aligned}0.35+0.65=1 \\\\ 0.95+0.05=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $\\bf{W}$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its third column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\bf{V}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029787b4-76ef-5324-83eb-649b506a66cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$, $v$, and $w$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244331} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc43066-87ae-5d14-b7df-35e4b5a96b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ and $v$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244559} {:answer/id #uuid "1f880ee7-2dae-5e94-a00e-cf7ea06127d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244592} {:answer/id #uuid "47d8a976-4e1b-5d5c-9400-17de622336ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244953} {:answer/id #uuid "66317c76-eb73-56c5-a0e6-948b81d5904d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ and $w$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d8a976-4e1b-5d5c-9400-17de622336ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244953} :answer-field/id #uuid "8587d707-0f0d-5a40-a9a9-e5a919395461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d6371d4-1a60-5526-b7b1-69a38ead3549" :question/math-academy-id "q-109881" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-0.45 \\\\ 1.55\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.5+0+0.5=1\n$$\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$ is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0+0=0\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$u$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14b2aa6-e2b0-5c7b-9b5e-bff935134b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121212} {:answer/id #uuid "ce803d77-1449-5c03-be82-10019ec069fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121213} {:answer/id #uuid "da0f9182-973c-5ad4-8864-b3f5bfe87290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$, $V$, and $W$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121214} {:answer/id #uuid "220b5ad9-a6a4-53ed-82b9-92706d35035d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121215} {:answer/id #uuid "5a819f20-4b26-5673-9f89-915cc0e71698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121216}] :answer-field/id #uuid "28b7af88-7cb5-53b2-af84-a7246e3059bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121211}] :question/id #uuid "8d2f0627-b325-5745-b223-6d5747b6cfb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109882" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$U = \\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, V = \\begin{bmatrix}0.45 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.55 & 0.75\\end{bmatrix}, W = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "492b45b4-10da-5362-ac90-bb5412259f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.265 \\\\ 0.735\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388384} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6667aa-28b0-525c-9069-3973c21dd227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.346 \\\\ 0.654\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388385} {:answer/id #uuid "c94cfbdf-e0f1-5ad7-b58a-42146e7370a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.145 \\\\ 0.855\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388386} {:answer/id #uuid "42ec7241-18a7-516f-909e-e9c55084fa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.325 \\\\ 0.675\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388387} {:answer/id #uuid "a30db03d-ef25-5ff9-9835-bf33eddfb7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.415 \\\\ 0.585\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ec7241-18a7-516f-909e-e9c55084fa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.325 \\\\ 0.675\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388387} :answer-field/id #uuid "1799f441-3ae2-50b8-8266-618df3f86647" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b120930-cc5f-5db6-89a1-4f05e7c988bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-135446" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.35 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.35 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.325 \\\\ 0.675\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1df1090c-b953-55e7-82db-2918444fb6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "405\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378666} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc961d6-6767-5034-8c94-13fc400c4870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "425\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378667} {:answer/id #uuid "cbec1301-90b2-5468-bdbd-75e91b591098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "395\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378668} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c54158-eb40-57d4-902a-43c93f2cbfcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "555\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378669} {:answer/id #uuid "07a27bf2-8db9-58f0-b441-14ea9ca218eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df1090c-b953-55e7-82db-2918444fb6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "405\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378666} :answer-field/id #uuid "c01d1ab0-b4e0-570d-9f6a-3444da987d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "960aa206-ef2f-590f-b6e6-46bfb1026352" :question/math-academy-id "q-135457" :question/problem "A certain company produces two types of footwear: casual and sports. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between both types of footwear each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Casual** | **Sports** |\n| To: | **Casual** | $0.55$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Sports** | $0.45$ | $0.3$ |  |\n\nThat is, $45%$ of casual customers switch to sports each year, and $70%$ of sports customers change to casual.\n\nCurrently, $700\\,000$ customers purchase casual footwear, while $300\\,000$ customers purchase sports footwear. How many customers will purchase sports footwear in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of footwear is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.595 \\\\ 0.405\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $40.5%$ of customers will purchase sports footwear. Computing $40.5%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.405=405\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $405\\,000$ customers will purchase sports footwear in one year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0455b8ee-0cb2-5011-aa4d-bae1103f59d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "390\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266179} {:answer/id #uuid "1f836c3a-c67b-5970-8731-c0f0a7334dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266420} {:answer/id #uuid "4593e854-e146-55e2-af50-0ca44d510660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "470\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266763} {:answer/id #uuid "cb506bd9-f1a3-567e-8cea-e083a2f8627e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267966} {:answer/id #uuid "cb83c181-c6fd-55f9-89d8-36bb89054cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "290\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb83c181-c6fd-55f9-89d8-36bb89054cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "290\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267968} :answer-field/id #uuid "0274237b-5707-50b2-a56c-b7645a561434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25a6f23d-99a0-510e-abf4-afb5461a1de7" :question/math-academy-id "q-135465" :question/problem "A certain company produces three types of ground coffee: fine, medium, and coarse. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between the three types of ground coffee each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Fine** | **Medium** | **Coarse** |\n| To: | **Fine** | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| **Medium** | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ |  |\n| **Coarse** | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |  |\n\nFor example, $30%$ of fine ground coffee customers switch to medium ground coffee each year, and $20%$ of coarse ground coffee customers switch to fine ground coffee.\n\nCurrently, $300\\,000$ customers buy fine ground coffee, $500\\,000$ customers buy medium ground coffee, and $200\\,000$ customers buy coarse ground coffee. How many customers will purchase fine ground coffee in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of ground coffee is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}300\\,000 \\\\ 500\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}300\\,000 \\\\ 500\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.47 \\\\ 0.24\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $29%$ of customers will buy fine ground coffee. Computing $29%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.29=290\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $290\\,000$ customers will buy fine ground coffee in one year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "474a8a35-2f0e-5821-afca-895b853e2f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$w$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266778} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a8a8f-bd88-5bd7-93f5-1f51e245d19b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267220} {:answer/id #uuid "a844b50d-312f-5ead-8e57-174902607b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267669} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1631ac-a4e6-5289-a648-1a896c779f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ and $v$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267823} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d91b88-d944-5bcf-aa2b-85fbc6643155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ and $w$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a844b50d-312f-5ead-8e57-174902607b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f7a808f-2559-583a-bc17-73f587979c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11a06254-1131-54e3-ac79-433bb7764638" :question/math-academy-id "q-135485" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}-0.2 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}0.15 \\\\ 0.95\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.15+0.95=1.1\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3ecc879-2c95-5f74-ac4a-ab969113e91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378680} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a103d0-014c-5342-a350-b00b3703cd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378681} {:answer/id #uuid "778b5f63-aa15-579f-aa01-22ef9920862f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.3$ | $0.6$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.7$ | $0.4$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378682} {:answer/id #uuid "11dc3d74-9a97-5c26-a835-b153e895787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378683} {:answer/id #uuid "e109ecab-31bf-5d0c-a848-783e513a6076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.7$ | $0.6$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3a103d0-014c-5342-a350-b00b3703cd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378681} :answer-field/id #uuid "81be96fa-a417-5d81-9fcf-9d833274bedd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df75b222-1f6c-5b44-9ba7-24d1998fa187" :question/math-academy-id "q-135491" :question/problem "In a particular town, the housekeepers use $2$ types of olive oil for preparing food: oil $A$ and oil $B.$  A study has shown that, each month \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B$, and\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these housekeepers change their preferences each month?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each month: \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B.$ This implies that $60%$ of them remain using oil $A.$\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$ This implies that $70%$ of them remain using oil $B.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c287be-ea57-55ce-baae-51bb45b38516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266167} {:answer/id #uuid "08deed52-4468-549e-81a6-f5ab7a3737e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266226} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac975b8-b27b-535d-a06f-1ef6ec9db9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266369} {:answer/id #uuid "50883166-e1a2-56c0-81b4-b76e3dee6317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} {:answer/id #uuid "db8543f6-e928-54f8-a113-98e22acbcee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50883166-e1a2-56c0-81b4-b76e3dee6317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed26647f-f52c-560b-b302-af5032a00378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40ee85ea-08ea-5955-8652-e4607e79ae86" :question/math-academy-id "q-135566" :question/problem "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daa07dd-689b-5d68-a711-77459bc9f7e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122079} {:answer/id #uuid "c40ed3ab-fd7f-589e-9bca-e8611878bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122080} {:answer/id #uuid "22e0d828-15f0-56a1-944a-243f28fd0241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122081} {:answer/id #uuid "44d59735-fe69-523e-810e-154c352fc2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122082} {:answer/id #uuid "45ca4e96-0cfd-54e5-a7fc-d0e7ec0255f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122083}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e3b787ef-0c6d-5613-ae18-c431681bcaa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122078}] :question/id #uuid "f54c1f29-b43d-5f0e-a558-1fd0e7509f92" :question/math-academy-id "q-35791" :question/problem "There are three groups of fans in a certain town: those who prefer basketball, those who prefer baseball, and those who prefer football. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the people that prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football,\n- from the people that prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball,\n- from the people that prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n\n$P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.4 & 0.15 & a \\\\ 0.32 & b & 0.65 \\\\ c & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e52049a5-38a6-5b70-94f2-c8d33b6dfa31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.24 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122133} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6f189e-0ccf-5e17-b8d8-91c3c77f90e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.12 \\\\ 0.52 \\\\ 0.36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122134} {:answer/id #uuid "24897b3f-8efe-5264-a980-ec873b08d162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 \\\\ 0.42 \\\\ 0.56\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122135} {:answer/id #uuid "2f89b864-8eed-51df-b4ea-ad31a13b8b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.24 \\\\ 0.32 \\\\ 0.44\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122136} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5df64b-b174-5071-8633-3bc92f288731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.28 \\\\ 0.38 \\\\ 0.34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122137}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9881a85c-e966-5649-976b-b7827ba47e48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122132}] :question/id #uuid "27eeb3bb-6a91-5ba8-9145-47e0dfe56bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35842" :question/problem "$P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}, x_{0} = \\begin{bmatrix}0.2 \\\\ 0.6 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector $x_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector $x_{1}$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758ee170-1fcb-5640-8b61-f22fb7a21811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "520\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322063} {:answer/id #uuid "936daf2f-be59-5538-b600-77f0341e8b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "400\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322316} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c760ab-015f-5f08-8419-73f7e6627df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "430\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322665} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8548e7-cae1-5bab-a94c-045833d4e0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322760} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b6826a-9e7d-507c-8455-dfd824432ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "640\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce8548e7-cae1-5bab-a94c-045833d4e0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322760} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe25491b-be23-5337-9805-76ec9cd44496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62389cec-4c75-591c-8976-ec4ed362e628" :question/math-academy-id "q-35845" :question/problem "A certain company produces two types of smartphones: Phone $A$ and Phone $B.$ The following table describes how the number of customers changes between both types of smartphones each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Phone $A$** | **Phone $B$** |\n| To: | **Phone $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Phone $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nThat is, $40%$ of Phone $A$ customers switch to Phone $B$ each year, and $30%$ of Phone $B$ customers switch to Phone $A.$\n\nCurrently, $600\\,000$ customers use Phone $A,$ while $400\\,000$ customers use Phone $B.$ How many customers will use Phone $A$ in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each smartphone is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.48 \\\\ 0.52\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $48%$ of customers will use Phone $A.$ Computing $48%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.48=480\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $480\\,000$ customers will use Phone $A$ in one year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5825d08-86a3-50d7-8984-8f2cd8d0faf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.393 \\\\ 0.607\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122151} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ad3b9e-20a5-5b74-9a37-9df7886cff6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122152} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7fb7ea-e2b3-5992-9bf6-e41c09e0cbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.611 \\\\ 0.389\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122153} {:answer/id #uuid "491996ac-bf8d-5eee-a987-0588261d1f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.442 \\\\ 0.558\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122154} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9686e5-79d6-5616-8acb-0e5b13b9ae3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.526 \\\\ 0.474\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122155}] :answer-field/id #uuid "98df5681-9ccd-5b69-82eb-39e17040c2c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da359ad7-2c5e-5f15-a2e5-6728987ffc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.393 \\\\ 0.607\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391939} {:answer/id #uuid "a65dbb5f-4e7c-55d0-9006-3317ba92c5a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.442 \\\\ 0.558\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391940} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca1d74f-f9fd-556b-a80a-717911ef4cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.526 \\\\ 0.474\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391941} {:answer/id #uuid "a42f9714-7fe1-502d-aca7-b5820479478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391942} {:answer/id #uuid "e7837d5a-4a5e-50f1-b388-732ea129adef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.611 \\\\ 0.389\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a42f9714-7fe1-502d-aca7-b5820479478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391942} :answer-field/id #uuid "424b0520-f951-5a27-8a16-c0b8ff12cee2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3da8136-058f-5b0b-abbd-f2c6d4a902e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35846" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.71\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.71\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
